# Intent: the unit's own music session runs in cycles for hours, like the host's (owner 2026-11-13: "i could be listening to music for hours and it should dance. it could take breaks and navigate through its slow start to full dance but it shouldnt just stop and never start again"). The plain C session machine now has the break (a dance block of 5 minutes charging or 2 minutes on battery, then 90 s of rest, then the dance again), a 60 s session gap (a song change keeps it), no hourly or daily caps; hal_music.cpp stops the dance on a break, ends everything on the end, sets the block length from the charging state and keeps the notes hopping.
# Upstream: MaiPai only (hal_music.cpp, maipai_music_judge.h). Applies after 123.
# Check after a flash: with Home stopped and Dance to music on, a long song: the nod, the dance after 20 s, a break after 2 or 5 minutes, the dance again 90 s later; serial lines "offline music: nod / dance / break / end".
